From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 13:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: qca8k: keep 802.1Q uppers under qca-8021q

When a port leaves a VLAN-aware bridge, or its bridge turns VLAN
filtering off, the DSA core takes the port's 802.1Q uppers out of the
switch and clears NETIF_F_HW_VLAN_CTAG_FILTER. Under qca-8021q an
upper's VLAN is the only way its frames reach the CPU, so lan2.35
stopped passing traffic, and an upper created afterwards was never
installed at all, until the port joined a VLAN-aware bridge again.

Opt in to ds->vlan_upper_filtering_always, added by the previous patch,
while the tagger is qca-8021q.

On a GL-B3000, lan2.35 pinging a peer on lan2, each step three times:
lan2 leaving a VLAN-aware bridge, an upper created on the standalone
port afterwards, a bridge turning VLAN filtering off and lan2 leaving
that bridge each went from 0/5 to 5/5. With lan2 in a VLAN-aware bridge
it was 5/5 before and after.

Signed-off-by: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/dsa/qca/qca8k-8xxx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/qca/qca8k-8xxx.c
@@ -2068,6 +2068,7 @@ static int qca8k_change_tag_protocol(str
 	case DSA_TAG_PROTO_QCA:
 		dsa_tag_8021q_unregister(ds);
 		qca8k_user_vlan_filter_feature(ds, false);
+		ds->vlan_upper_filtering_always = false;
 		priv->tag_proto = proto;
 
 		ret = qca8k_set_tag_8021q_vlan_mode(priv, false);
@@ -2106,6 +2107,12 @@ static int qca8k_change_tag_protocol(str
 		if (ret)
 			goto restore_vlan;
 		qca8k_user_vlan_filter_feature(ds, true);
+		/* Leaving a VLAN-aware bridge, or the bridge turning VLAN
+		 * filtering off, must not take the port's 802.1Q uppers out of
+		 * the switch: under tag_8021q an upper's VLAN is how its frames
+		 * reach the CPU at all.
+		 */
+		ds->vlan_upper_filtering_always = true;
 		return 0;
 	default:
 		return -EPROTONOSUPPORT;
